{# table; title: Installation; category: docs #}

  I. Requirements

-  Neovim 0.11 or later (0.12 recommended)
-  A C compiler (`cc`, `gcc`, `clang`, `cl` or `zig`) and the `tree-sitter` command, only to build the grammar the first time (the plugin does it, see below)
-  `libsqlite3`, the library of the index. The plugin uses it through LuaJIT and has no Lua dependency. If it is not found by the system loader,
   point `vim.g.sqlite_clib_path` at it
-  Optional: `pandoc` for exporting to LaTeX, PDF, Word, OpenDocument and EPUB; the `latex` tree-sitter parser for highlighting math; a Nerd Font for the icons of
   checkboxes and concealed queries (without one the icons are plain symbols)


  II. Installation methods

Any package manager works. Some examples:

-  {@ link, https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim; desc: lazy.nvim @} (recommended)

###  src lua
return {
  'Loreite/fey.nvim',
  event = 'VeryLazy',
  config = function()
    require('fey').setup({
      fey_court_dir = '~/feyhollow',
    })
    -- Experimental LSP support
    vim.lsp.enable('fey')
  end,
}
###

-  vim.pack (Neovim 0.12 and later)

###  src lua
vim.pack.add({
  { src = 'https://github.com/Loreite/fey.nvim' },
})
require('fey').setup({ fey_court_dir = '~/feyhollow' })
vim.lsp.enable('fey')
###

-  {@ link, https://github.com/lewis6991/pckr.nvim; desc: pckr.nvim @}

###  src lua
require('pckr').add({
  {
    'Loreite/fey.nvim',
    config = function() require('fey').setup({ fey_court_dir = '~/feyhollow' }) end,
  },
})
###

-  {@ link, https://github.com/junegunn/vim-plug; desc: vim-plug @}

###  src vim
Plug 'Loreite/fey.nvim'

lua << EOF
require('fey').setup({ fey_court_dir = '~/feyhollow' })
EOF
###


  III. The grammar

The first time a Fey file is opened the plugin builds the tree-sitter grammar of Fey and installs it in its own folder. If that fails (no compiler), or you
want to build it yourself, run `:Fey install_treesitter_grammar`; `:checkhealth fey` says which grammar is found, where, and whether it is the version the plugin
needs. See {@ link, troubleshoot.fey; desc: Troubleshooting @} for problems on Windows.


  IV. The first hollow

Open Neovim in a folder of notes (or an empty folder) and run `:FeyHollowInit`. The folder becomes a hollow: a `.fey` folder is made with the index and the hollow is
registered in the court. From then on the agenda, the queries and the links read it. The court folder (`fey_court_dir`) is made the first time it is needed, with the
agenda inbox in it; `<Leader>;c` captures a note into it.

Every file ending in `.fey` is a note; a file ending in `.fey_archive` is an archive. Folders listed in `vault.ignore` are not indexed.


  V. Next

{@ link, tutorial.fey; desc: The tutorial @} walks through the features with a small set of notes, {@ link, configuration.fey; desc: Configuration @} lists every option.
